<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
  <div class="theme-card p-4 md:p-6">
    <div class="mb-6">
      <div class="theme-section-label mono mb-2">Legal</div>
      <h1 class="bebas mb-2 text-3xl leading-none md:text-4xl">Terms of service</h1>
      <p class="theme-subtitle mb-0">A lightweight launch version of terms. Review with counsel before commercial release.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-5 text-sm leading-7 text-zinc-300">
      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">1. Service</h2>
        <p><%= theme_app_name %> helps users track dart matches and related statistics.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">2. Accounts</h2>
        <p>Users are responsible for the accuracy of account details and for safeguarding login access.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">3. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Do not misuse the service, disrupt infrastructure, scrape data without permission, or attempt unauthorized access.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">4. Availability</h2>
        <p>The service may change, pause, or be removed. Add any SLA or paid-plan commitments here if needed.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">5. User content</h2>
        <p>Users keep ownership of names and data they enter, but grant you the rights needed to operate the service.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">6. Liability</h2>
        <p>Add your jurisdiction-specific limitation of liability, warranty disclaimer, and mandatory consumer law wording.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-white">7. Governing law</h2>
        <p>State the governing law, venue, and any consumer-specific rights that cannot be waived under EU law.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
